The fixed semantics already models exactly the needed primitives: string iteration, `list(str)`, `sorted(list-of-str)`, and string `join`. I’m using a single character loop so the unbounded-domain induction follows the string’s recursive code sequence directly; the trusted `sortVS` primitive remains isolated to sorting each completed word.
