The concrete run passed all prompt examples plus empty and repeated-space cases. The remaining proof engineering issue is allocator freshness: every word flush creates two temporary lists that persist in the modeled heap, so the loop invariant must track the monotone heap domain as well as the string result. I’m checking the available Map/Set hooks before choosing the smallest sound invariant.
