The hooked `Map` sort cannot carry a stable constructor without introducing an operational heap abstraction that the validator would reject. I’m dropping that route and removing list allocation from the implementation entirely. The replacement keeps each current word sorted by inserting every non-space character into its proper position using string slicing; this trades heap bookkeeping for a second, fully symbolic loop invariant over immutable strings.
