codex
The diagnostic confirmed that the inner claim was sound but unnecessarily included the entire outer continuation, so proving it in isolation unrolled the outer loop. I’m separating it into a true auxiliary theorem: it will summarize only the insertion loop’s local-state transformation under an arbitrary continuation. The outer result relation will compose that insertion result existentially with the remaining outer scan.
